\chapter{Editor integrations and the repository knowledge service}
\label{ch:69}
\index{Editor integrations and the repository knowledge service}

Editor packages provide On1x source and interface highlighting for the documented editors. The optional stdio language server wraps compiler diagnostics and formatting. Its implemented features and settings should be read from the LSP addon rather than inferred from language servers for other languages. When diagnostics differ from the command line, compare working directory, executable, import roots and enabled actions.

The knowledge addon under \OnxCodeTerm{on1x/addons/mcp} serves read-only repository evidence. It has a bounded evidence model including source references and distinctions among discovery, contracts, implementation and admission. A server response can help a reader find a supporting manual, but it does not compile code, perform a dependency build, or grant foreign admission. Deployment, service authorization, and the contents of the startup snapshot are separate choices. Test editor behavior and addon package behavior using their own fixtures.

\section{Follow two versions of one buffer}
Save a syntactically complete function with a wrong return type. The editor
may show no diagnostic even when the build rejects the function. On save the
server invokes dependency inspection with JSON diagnostics; the compiler
scans, parses and resolves modules, without doing ordinary type checking.
Now remove a required delimiter and save again. With JSON reporting enabled,
a parser error in the saved entry can be published at the reported byte
offset, converted to the client's position encoding. A dependency error is
logged rather than attached to an arbitrary position in the entry.

Restore the delimiter in memory without saving and request formatting.
Formatting parses a private copy of this new text and returns an edit; it
does not format the stale on-disk version. Conversely, save diagnostics
for the older revision should not remain actionable after this edit. This
explains why a formatting preview can succeed after a failed save, before
the disk file has been repaired. Neither outcome establishes the return
type; the ordinary compiler check is the appropriate next observation.

For a repository question, imagine looking up a kernel header and then
editing its documentation. The knowledge service answers from the allowed
bytes loaded at startup. A subsequent query to that running service does
not reread the edit. Refreshing a reviewed snapshot can change the answer
without any change to the editor buffer or the compiler executable. Record
the source reference returned with the answer when distinguishing these cases.

